## 🚀 Getting Started

This project was generated with [`kagent`](https://github.com/kagent-dev/kagent).

### Prerequisites

- [Go](https://golang.org/doc/install) (1.23 or later)
- [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/)

### Local Development

1.  **Tidy dependencies:**
    ```bash
    go mod tidy
    ```

2.  **Run the server:**
    ```bash
    go run main.go
    ```

### Building the Docker Image

To build a Docker image for this project, run:

```bash
kagent mcp build
```

This will create an image named `{{.ProjectName}}:latest`.

### Deploying

Deploy the built image on your container platform, expose its HTTP MCP endpoint,
and register that endpoint in kagent with a `RemoteMCPServer`.

```bash
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 {{.ProjectName}}:latest --http :8080
```

## 🛠️ Adding a New Tool

To add a new tool to your project, use the `kagent mcp add-tool` command:

```bash
kagent mcp add-tool <tool-name>
```

This will generate a new Go file in the `tools/` directory with a template for your new tool. You will need to add the new tool to the `main.go` file.
